! xterm's defaults in the window server's desktop (tools/x/desktop points XAPPLRESDIR here), on top of
! Debian's own /etc/X11/app-defaults/XTerm.
!
! The clipboard with the keys Konsole has: Ctrl-Shift-C copies the selection to the clipboard (and from there
! to the host's), Ctrl-Shift-V pastes the clipboard (the page puts the host's clipboard there first). On a Mac,
! Cmd-C and Cmd-V are these keys in a terminal. Selecting with the mouse and pasting with the middle button
! (the primary selection) is xterm's own and stays as it is.
*VT100.translations: #override \n\
	Shift Ctrl <Key>C: copy-selection(CLIPBOARD) \n\
	Shift Ctrl <Key>V: insert-selection(CLIPBOARD)
